# `$isAsBorn` takes a maker whose literal holds values that are no constants (NewObject, FinishObject, Return), and one whose literal is written with `__proto__: null`: an emitter's table.
# The usual prototype of a literal's layout is Object.prototype, so an object born without one stands "below another prototype"; for such a maker the stamped form bears the flag isBornWithoutPrototype and the emitter asks the structure's prototype for null.
# "As born" stays exact both ways: the two makers share one layout; an object of the one asked against the other gets a no. One whose link was taken away is as one born without (LINKTAKENAWAY); one that was given Object.prototype later stays a no (GIVENTHEUSUALLINK): false says nothing. A literal written below anything else names no layout.
